+**The setup currently in use is a demo setup, not a ceremony.**
+
+| Phase | What was used | Standing |
+|---|---|---|
+| Phase 1 (universal) | `powersOfTau28_hez_final_14.ptau` — Polygon Hermez perpetual Powers of Tau, 54 contributors plus a public beacon | Sound. Reused as-is. |
+| Phase 2 (circuit-specific) | One contribution, named `aperture-mpp-1777587329`, with no beacon | **Demo only.** |
+
+Phase 2 is sound only if at least one contributor destroyed their toxic
+waste. One contribution and no beacon reduces that to a single machine:
+whoever held the entropy can forge a proof for any statement, including
+`is_compliant = 1` on a payment that breaks the policy.
+
+Confirm it against the shipped zkey rather than taking our word for it:
+
+```bash
+node ../../../mandate/circuits/scripts/inspect-zkey-setup.mjs ../../services/prover-service/artifacts/payment.zkey
+# phase-2 contributions    1
+# beacon applied           no
+```
+
+The hello-world commands earlier in this file are local and discard-only —
+they are a toolchain check, never a setup for anything that holds value.
+
+A public multi-party phase-2 ceremony is planned. Phase 1 will be reused
+unchanged; only phase 2 is redone, with contributions collected in the open,
+a beacon whose source is announced beforehand, and published transcripts a
+third party can replay. Until it lands and its verifying key is deployed,
+this setup is called a demo everywhere it appears.

